    {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_541daf45949b4fb581801af3",
      "name": "semantic_search",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"count\": 77, \"items_by_type\": {\"table\": [{\"id\": \"SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE\", \"desc\": \"Space supervisor usage fact table: one row per supervisor (MIT_ID) recording how much space they supervise and for how many departments: department count, department DLC key list (comma-separated when multiple), number of supervisees, supervised square footage, research volume, and derived ratio measures (sqft per supervisee, sqft per research volume, research volume per sqft). Joins to SPACE_UNIT and other DLC-carrying tables via DEPT_NAMES = DLC_KEY (only single-department rows match); used for supervisor space-usage and research-volume statistics per department/DLC.\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_DETAIL\", \"desc\": \"Space assignment detail fact table: one row per physical room assigned to a space unit, with building/floor/space-unit/space-usage keys, room identifiers (building-room number and name, room number), room square footage, room counter, and building component. Used to count rooms per space unit or per building, and to analyze room size and usage distribution. Joins to SPACE_UNIT via SPACE_UNIT_KEY, FCLT_BUILDING via BUILDING_KEY, SPACE_FLOOR via FLOOR_KEY, and SPACE_USAGE via SPACE_USAGE_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_UNIT\", \"desc\": \"Space unit dimension table: one row per space unit (an organizational space-assignment unit such as a department, program, or office that receives space allocation), with space unit key/code, space unit name, the facilities organization it belongs to, and DLC key. Bridges FCLT_ORGANIZATION (organization attribution) and SPACE_DETAIL (rooms assigned to the space unit); used to group room counts and space statistics by space unit.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION\", \"desc\": \"Facilities organization dimension table: one row per organization in the institute's hierarchical organization tree (levels 1-6, from institute-wide down to sub-units), with organization identifiers and names, parent and major-organization attribution, hierarchy level, assignable-space flag, course number for academic departments, description, DLC (department/lab/center) key and name, and cross-references to HR organization units. Parent of SPACE_UNIT (space assigned to organizations) and referenced by FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY for room occupancy attribution.\"}, {\"id\": \"ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD\", \"desc\": \"Space-planning room load table: one row per room record from the space planning feed, with the building-room identifier, building component, floor (numeric or label such as 'G9'), space usage text (e.g. 'DSGN STUDIO', 'CONF RM'), space unit code, HR organization unit id, and room access level. Links rooms to SPACE_UNIT via SPACE_UNIT_CODE and to FCLT_ORGANIZATION/HR_ORG_UNIT via HR_ORG_UNIT_ID; used for floor/access-level/space-usage room analysis from the space-planning perspective, without the area and use-key columns carried by FCLT_ROOMS.\"}, {\"id\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT\", \"desc\": \"HR organization unit dimension table: one row per HR organization unit with unit key/ID/title, unit level classification (ALL MIT, TOP LEVEL, DEPARTMENTS, SUB DEPARTMENT, ORGANIZATION LEVEL, NON HIERARCHY ORG UNITS), HR department identifiers and name variants (short, long, alphabetical), organization hierarchy area names (school area, top level, root), the full HR hierarchy path levels 1-7 (each with ID, sort order, and name), and DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME cross-references to departments/labs/centers. Joined from FCLT_ORGANIZATION and MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY via DLC_KEY to attach HR department attributes (title, level, department name, long name, hierarchy path) to facilities organizations and DLCs; a single DLC_KEY can map to multiple HR org unit rows, so joins via DLC_KEY may fan out.\"}, {\"id\": \"BUILDINGS\", \"desc\": \"Space-domain building lookup table: one row per building with building key/number, building name, street and mailing addresses as single text fields, gross and assignable square footage (in square feet), and a building counter. Referenced by SPACE_DETAIL via BUILDING_KEY; a lightweight building reference for space-assignment reporting, without the type/ownership/site classification carried by FCLT_BUILDING or FAC_BUILDING.\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_USAGE\", \"desc\": \"Space usage classification lookup table: one row per space usage key with its usage name (e.g. classroom, office, lab usage categories). Referenced by SPACE_DETAIL via SPACE_USAGE_KEY to decode the usage classification of assigned rooms.\"}, {\"id\": \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY\", \"desc\": \"Master department hierarchy table: one row per department/lab/center (DLC) under the 'Standard Hierarchy' hierarchy type, recording the DLC key/code/name and its five-level hierarchy path from the institute root (level 1 'All Departments') through executive areas down to the DLC's placement, with each level's code and name (null for levels deeper than the DLC's position). Joins to HR_ORG_UNIT and FCLT_ORGANIZATION via DLC_KEY; used to report or filter the master-hierarchy placement (school/area path) of a DLC, and as a DLC scope filter when only DLCs present in the standard hierarchy should be included.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_BUILDING_HIST\", \"desc\": \"Historical facilities building snapshot table: one row per building per fiscal period (FISCAL_PERIOD in YYYYMM format, covering 201505-201906, 48 periods, ~255 buildings), preserving each building's attributes over time: identifiers and names, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, site, campus sector, access level, building type, ownership type, use, occupancy class, height, cost center/collector references, coordinates, and number of rooms. Used for fiscal-period building history analysis (area/room-count trends, dispersion statistics across historical records); use FCLT_BUILDING for the current snapshot. Date columns (DATE_BUILT/DATE_ACQUIRED/DATE_OCCUPIED) are stored in MM/DD/YYYY format; FCLT_BUILDING_HIST_1 is the variant storing them in DD-MON-YY format.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\", \"desc\": \"Subject-level summary fact table per term: one row per subject (or cluster) per term with department/school attribution, unit structure (total/lecture/lab/prep/design units), and detailed enrollment statistics including final enrollment, first-week and fifth-week enrollment, and credit/listener splits at both subject and cluster level. Used for enrollment and unit statistics by department, school, term, and subject group.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_BUILDING\", \"desc\": \"Facilities building inventory table: one row per physical building with building number/name, type (e.g. ACADEMIC), ownership, use, occupancy class, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, number of rooms, key dates (built/acquired/occupied), site and geographic coordinates. Parent of FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY\", \"desc\": \"Student directory table: one row per student with name components, full name, office location and phone, email address, department code and department name, and student year. The DEPARTMENT column stores the academic department code and joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE, enabling per-department student counts.\"}, {\"id\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW\", \"desc\": \"Newer HR organization unit dimension table: one row per HR organization unit with the same unit/department identity and hierarchy-path structure as HR_ORG_UNIT (unit key/ID/title/level, HR department code and name variants, school-area/top-level/root names, hierarchy path levels 1-5, DLC_KEY) but a shallower hierarchy path (levels 6-7 absent), no HR_DEPARTMENT_ID and no DLC_NAME column, and an extra HR_DEPARTMENT_ABBR abbreviation column. Holds more unit rows than HR_ORG_UNIT (691 vs 641, including units absent from HR_ORG_UNIT); use HR_ORG_UNIT when DLC_NAME or the deeper hierarchy path is required, HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW for the newer unit coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_MAJOR_USE\", \"desc\": \"Facilities major use classification lookup table (FCLT family): one row per major use code (e.g. CLASSRMS classrooms, OFFICES offices, LABS laboratories, RESIDENT residential) with its short code, description, and assignable-space flag. Joined from FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_MAJOR_USE_KEY to decode a room's major use; current snapshot only, use FCLT_MAJOR_USE_HIST for fiscal-period historical variants.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_FLOOR_HIST\", \"desc\": \"Historical facilities floor table: one row per floor per fiscal period (FISCAL_PERIOD in YYYYMM format, covering 201505-201602), preserving each floor's number/label, gross, assignable and non-assignable areas, sort sequence, level, wing, and access level over time. Fiscal-period counterpart of FCLT_FLOOR; joins to buildings via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY and to current floor records via FCLT_FLOOR_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ROOMS_HIST\", \"desc\": \"Historical facilities room table: one row per room per fiscal period (FISCAL_PERIOD in YYYYMM format; current data covers period 201505), preserving each room's identifiers, floor, use classifications, organization assignment, area, access level, and coordinates over time. Fiscal-period counterpart of FCLT_ROOMS; joins to current room records via FCLT_ROOM_KEY and to buildings via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_FLOOR\", \"desc\": \"Facilities floor inventory table: one row per floor of a building (floor key formatted '<building key>-<floor>'), with floor number/label, gross, assignable and non-assignable areas of the floor, sort sequence, level identifier, building wing, and access level. Child of FCLT_BUILDING via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY and parent of FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_FLOOR_KEY; used for per-floor area aggregation and floor-level filtering (e.g. floors with assignable area above a threshold).\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_FLOOR\", \"desc\": \"Space-domain floor lookup table: one row per floor key with the floor number/label and floor name. Referenced by SPACE_DETAIL via FLOOR_KEY to attach floor identity to assigned rooms; a lightweight floor reference without the area measures carried by FCLT_FLOOR or FAC_FLOOR.\"}, {\"id\": \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT\", \"desc\": \"SIS administrative department table with administrative department code/name, phone area code and phone number, and clearing cost collector. Joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT via SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE = DEPARTMENT_CODE for department contact information.\"}], \"metric\": [{\"id\": \"dw_2896\", \"desc\": \"For each facility organization, show the research volume, department names, square footage, MIT ID, and the average square footage in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows (grouped by facility organization key and ordered by research volume) for space supervisor usage records where the number of supervisees is 2, and only include those records where the average square footage in the window is greater than 200. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4452\", \"desc\": \"For each department in the \\\"Provost Area\\\" that is associated with a space unit with space unit code 97500, show the department code, department name, school area name, the rank of each department within its school area based on department code, the corresponding DLC name, the space unit name, space unit code, associated organization name, department count, number of supervisees, and the highest research volume ever recorded for each department count group. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4025\", \"desc\": \"For rooms with a square footage of 150, show the space unit code, space unit name, and the maximum rank within each space unit code group, and for each of those space units, show the major organization, top-level HR organization name, HR department name, the average, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the organization numbers for each HR department name, considering only organizations that are assignable and have a non-null organization number. The results should include the space unit code, space unit name, maximum rank, major organization, top-level HR organization name, HR department name, average organization number, organization number variance, and organization number standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4061\", \"desc\": \"For each department and academic year, show the department name, academic year, academic year description, and the geometric mean of the total units for all subjects offered by the department in regular terms with total units greater than zero, along with, for each academic building where these subjects are held and which has rooms larger than 40 square meters, the building name, the average, range, and variance of the room areas, as well as the total assignable area of the building and the year the building was built. The results are ordered by department name, academic year (descending), and room area range (descending). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3235\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and its corresponding facility organization key where the department is in the Provost Area, provide the number of organizations, the minimum department hierarchy level 3 code, the range, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of HR organization units per facility organization (considering only those with a non-null DLC key and where the hierarchy type is 'Standard Hierarchy'), listing the results in order by department name and facility organization key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1393\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year and department in Mathematics, what is the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered in that year and department (considering only subjects offered in the current term, with more than 0 total units, and with subject enrollment number greater than the average for that department and year), and for those departments, what are the department code, corresponding administrative department name, the graduate level of courses, and the total number of distinct courses per department, for all degree-granting departments except the Management department? Present the results as academic year, department name, total units variance, total units standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), department code, administrative department name, graduate level, and number of distinct courses, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_488\", \"desc\": \"Among all academic buildings at MIT, which building use type has the largest variance in room area, and what is the name of the building with the largest total room area for that use type? Show the building use, the area variance, and the building name with the largest total room area for that use type. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4612\", \"desc\": \"For each organization whose parent is 'S H&SS' and that is associated with a space unit with space unit code 97500, list the organization name, description, HR org unit title, row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the organization name, the space unit name, space unit code, department count, number of supervisees, the average department count within each department count group ordered by number of supervisees, and the total square footage for each organization. Include subtotals for each organization (the corresponding organization name field is 'SUBTOTAL') and a grand total across all organizations (the corresponding organization name field is 'TOTAL'). Do not repeat the organization name if it is the same as the previous row. Sort the table by organization name and space unit name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1488\", \"desc\": \"For each academic building at MIT and each of its floors with total assignable area greater than 5000 and at least one room with access level 1 or 2, provide the building's long name, the floor number, the range and variance of the area of rooms on that floor (considering only rooms with access level 1 or 2), the range and variance of the assignable area of its floors that have at least one room, and the total number of rooms in the building. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3410\", \"desc\": \"For rooms with an area greater than 300 and located in buildings with more than 100 rooms, show the building's long name, the room's full name, the room's area, and the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the building's long name, along with the name of the space unit, the associated organization name, and both the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the organization numbers for all organizations linked to that space unit (considering only space units with a non-null DLC key and organizations with assignable status), where the room and the space unit share the same organization key. List the columns in the following order: building's long name, room's full name, room's area, window row number, space unit name, organization name, organization number variance, and organization number standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_12\", \"desc\": \"For each building type, show the building type name, the ownership type, and calculate the average, range, and variance of the number of rooms in building history records for buildings of that type and ownership type that are located on the MIT site, but exclude buildings that are classified as residential. For each building type, include a grand total for all ownership types in the format of (building type, null, total statistics). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1465\", \"desc\": \"For each department in the Provost Area at the School of Science level, excluding the Biology department, and for each organization within those departments (excluding organizations with IDs '138' and '250'), show the department name, department code, organization name, organization ID, the maximum average organization number within each department code group, and the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the area of rooms assigned to the organization (considering only organizations with more than 5 rooms and excluding organizations named 'ADMISSIONS'), ordered by department name and organization name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2958\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, among subjects that are not repeatable, what is the average, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by each department? List the academic year, department name, average enrollment, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), ordered by variance descending. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1190\", \"desc\": \"For each building where the building type is 'ACADEMIC', the building is not the Brown Building, and the building has more than 3 historical records, give the building name, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the assignable area across its historical records, the average area of its rooms, and the variance of the area of its rooms, including only buildings that are academic buildings or have building number '32'. List the results in descending order of the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the assignable area. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4271\", \"desc\": \"For rooms on floor 2 with access level 1, show the space unit, the maximum row number (within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by building room) for each space unit, the building room, the organization name, the department name, and the difference between the access level of the room and the average access level for that department. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1864\", \"desc\": \"For each organization whose organization level is 5 and is not 'ADMISSIONS', and for each organization and its corresponding HR department where the organization is assignable, the HR organization unit level is 'DEPARTMENTS', the organization is not 'Cambridge-MIT Institute', and the organization is in the 'Provost Area' top-level HR hierarchy, but excluding organizations with organization IDs '138' and '250', show the organization name, description, the corresponding space unit name, the total number of space units associated with each organization, the HR department name, the number of organizations, and the minimum organization number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2616\", \"desc\": \"For each space unit with a room square footage greater than 100, what is the building room, building room name, space usage, the number of distinct floors it appears on, and the total room counter, but only include those where the total room counter is greater than the average room counter across all space units with room square footage greater than 100? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1357\", \"desc\": \"For each access level code and campus sector, what is the access level code, access level name, campus sector, the variance of the number of rooms in the building history for buildings with a nonzero number of rooms, assignable area greater than 0, and that are residential buildings at MIT, as well as, for each floor in the Fairchild Building with access level 1 or 2 and in academic buildings, the floor number, the building's long name, the range and variance of the area of rooms on that floor? Only include buildings that are at MIT. Also, include subtotals for each access level code (the corresponding campus sector field is 'SUBTOTAL') and a grand total across all access level codes (the corresponding campus sector field is 'TOTAL'). Do not repeat the access level code if it is the same as the previous row. Sort the table by access level code, campus sector, and floor. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2597\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, what is the description of the academic year, the department name, the average total units for all subjects offered by that department in terms that match that academic year and have a term status indicator of 'P', and the deviation of each department's average total units from the overall average total units for that academic year? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1833\", \"desc\": \"For each department and subject grade type where the subject is offered in the current academic year, is letter graded, and the department is Mathematics (Course 18), provide the number of subjects, the minimum total units, the school name, the department phone number, the organization name, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the areas of its rooms, and the department's DLC name, including subtotals for each department (the corresponding department field is 'SUBTOTAL') and a grand total across all departments (the corresponding department field is 'TOTAL'). Do not repeat the department if it is the same as the previous row. Only include organizations that have more than 5 rooms, are associated with a non-null DLC key, and are not the 'ADMISSIONS' department or the 'Political Science' department. Sort the table by department, grade type, and descending standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of room areas. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}], \"concept\": [{\"id\": \"concept_room_space_inventory\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the physical room inventory and its space assignment: SPACE_DETAIL (rooms assigned to space units with usage classification and square footage), FCLT_ROOMS (facilities room inventory with use classifications, organization assignment, and area in square meters), FAC_ROOMS (the FAC_* family room snapshot with the same structure as FCLT_ROOMS but FAC_* keys), and ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD (space-planning room load feed with floor, space usage text, access level, and space unit code / HR org unit id links). They jointly answer questions about how many rooms exist, room sizes, room usage, and which organization/space unit occupies rooms, but differ in assignment perspective, key family, and area units.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_space_unit_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Space unit lookup tables identifying the organizational units that receive space allocation: SPACE_UNIT (with FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY organization attribution) and SPACE_UNIT2 (identity/name only). They answer the same space-unit identity questions but differ in organization linkage and coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_dept_hr_org_hierarchy\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing the institute's department/lab/center (DLC) and HR organization hierarchies: the HR organization unit dimension in two feed variants (HR_ORG_UNIT, HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW), the master department standard hierarchy path (MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY), its DLC-to-administrative-object link table (MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS), and the direct-parent department lookup (MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT). They jointly answer questions about which HR department/area a DLC or organization belongs to, the hierarchy path or parent of a department, and HR department names/codes/levels, and are joined to FCLT_ORGANIZATION via DLC_KEY for facilities/space attribution. They differ in hierarchy representation (full path vs direct parent vs HR unit attributes), unit coverage, and companion columns.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_building_inventory\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the physical building inventory and its attributes (number/name, type, ownership, site, campus sector, access level, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, number of rooms, key dates): the current FCLT_* family snapshot, its fiscal-period history (in two date-format variants), the FAC_* family snapshot, and the lightweight space-domain building lookup. They jointly answer questions about building characteristics, areas, and room counts, but differ in time coverage, table family, attribute richness, and area units.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_department_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Lookup tables describing academic departments and their school attribution: the SIS department dimension, the student-facing department lookup, and the SIS administrative department (contact information). They answer questions about department names, full names, school code/name, degree-granting status, budget codes, and department phone numbers, but differ in attribute coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_floor_inventory\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the floor level of buildings: the current FCLT_* family floor inventory with floor areas, the FAC_* family floor snapshot with the same structure, the fiscal-period historical floor table, and the lightweight space-domain floor lookup. They jointly answer questions about floor numbers and per-floor assignable/non-assignable areas, but differ in time coverage, table family, and attribute richness.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_facility_organization_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Organization dimension tables describing the institute's hierarchical organization tree used for facilities/space attribution: FCLT_ORGANIZATION (keyed by FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY, with DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME) and FAC_ORGANIZATION (keyed by ORGANIZATION_KEY, with D_CODE). They answer the same questions about organization names, hierarchy levels, parent/major organizations, assignable flags, and HR cross-references, but belong to different table families and coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_room_major_use_classification\", \"desc\": \"Lookup tables classifying rooms by major use (classrooms, offices, laboratories, residential, circulation, etc.) with a short code, description, and assignable-space flag. They cover the current classification in the FCLT and FAC table families and the fiscal-period historical classification in the FCLT family, jointly answering questions about what a room is primarily used for and whether that use counts as assignable space.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_person_directory\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing people of the institute keyed by MIT_ID: the primary employee directory (contact details, titles, HR department), the Drupal-sourced employee feed (employee group/type, appointment flags, HR org unit), the person master table (payroll rank, position title, active flag), the HR faculty roster (appointment type, terminal degree, emeritus status), the OPA current-person snapshot (HR job/appointment attributes, faculty flag, sabbatical), and the student directory (students with department attribution and student year). They jointly answer questions about who a person is, their contact details, job/appointment attributes, and whether they are employee, faculty, or student; responsible faculty in subject offering tables resolve to these tables via RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_MIT_ID = MIT_ID.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_subject_offering_facts\", \"desc\": \"Fact tables recording subjects offered per term from different business processes: the course catalog (planned catalog attributes), the registrar's section/subject offering records (actual sections and enrollment), subject-level summaries (final enrollment statistics), the textbook information program (subjects tracked for course materials), and library reserve processing (subjects with library reserve activity). They share subject identity (SUBJECT_ID, TERM_CODE) and department attribution but differ in granularity, enrollment semantics, and available measures.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_time_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Time dimension tables of the warehouse at three granularities: TIME_DAY (one row per calendar date, with fiscal/calendar year and period, academic year, financial aid year, day of week, and the academic term code/description of the day), TIME_MONTH (one row per fiscal period in YYYYMM format, covering fiscal years 1996-2035, with fiscal quarter, calendar month, academic term, and financial aid year mappings), and TIME_QUARTER (one row per fiscal quarter, covering fiscal years 2000-2035, with quarter dates, payroll certification deadlines, and quarter status flags). They jointly answer questions about when fiscal periods/quarters/days run, which fiscal/calendar/academic year a date or month belongs to, and how day-level records roll up to months and quarters. They link to each other via FISCAL_PERIOD (day-month), FY_QUARTER_CODE (month-quarter), and FISCAL_YEAR (month-quarter association within the same fiscal year, fanning out months across all quarters of the year), and to the academic term tables via TIME_DAY.ACADEMIC_TERM_CODE or TIME_MONTH.ACADEMIC_TERM = TERM_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_building_address\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the postal/street addresses of buildings: the current FCLT_* family address table (multiple purpose-typed address rows per building), its fiscal-period historical counterpart, the FAC_* family address snapshot, and the single-text address fields of the space-domain BUILDINGS lookup. They jointly answer questions about where a building is located (street number/name, city, state, postal code), but differ in time coverage, address decomposition, and table family.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_academic_term_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing academic terms and their calendar/status attributes. They jointly answer questions about when terms run, which academic/financial-aid/degree year a term belongs to, and whether a term is current, previous, future, or regular. Coverage differs: the full historical term list, the status-tracked term subset, and the three-row relative term parameter reference.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_course_material_programs\", \"desc\": \"Tables covering course material provisioning: the Textbook Information Program (TIP) tracking textbook adoption status per subject offering, and library reserve processing tracking catalog items placed on reserve for subjects. They jointly answer questions about which subjects have course materials/textbooks, material status (TIP statuses such as 'RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options; library statuses such as 'U' Unknown, 'Y' Required Course Material), ISBNs, record counts, and reserve catalog item attributes. The two programs are linked by SUBJECT_ID + TERM_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_iap_activities\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing Independent Activities Period (IAP) activities offered in January terms: activity details (title, enrollment type, max enrollment, fee, cancellation flags), sessions (location, date, times), sponsors (name, type), categories, and persons. They jointly answer questions about IAP activity counts, enrollment capacity, fees, session scheduling, and sponsorship.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_course_catalog_sources\", \"desc\": \"Tables providing catalog-level subject attributes (titles, unit structure, grading rules, HGN level, requirement attributes, offering-term flags) from different source systems: the warehouse course catalog, the CIS course catalog feed, and the Drupal course catalog feed. They answer the same catalog-attribute questions but differ in source system, extra columns, and join paths to department/subject-code lookups.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_moira_mailing_lists\", \"desc\": \"Tables of the Moira mailing-list/group domain: the list master (one row per list with name, description, active flag, and type flags such as mailing list, group, NFS group, public, hidden), the membership detail (one row per list member with member login, full name, MIT ID, and last update date), and the owner lookup (one row per owner entity with owner name and owner type LIST/USER/KERBEROS). They jointly answer questions about which lists exist and their properties, who belongs to a list, and who owns a list; MOIRA_LIST is the parent of MOIRA_LIST_DETAIL via MOIRA_LIST_KEY, and MOIRA_LIST_OWNER is referenced by MOIRA_LIST_DETAIL via MOIRA_LIST_OWNER_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_cip_program_classification\", \"desc\": \"Lookup tables of the Classification of Instructional Programs (CIP) used to classify courses/instructional programs into two-digit categories, four-digit series, and six-digit program codes, with revision version years (1990/2000/2010/2020). CIP holds the current single-version classification (one row per program code, with a change NOTE), while CIP_WITH_VERSION preserves every revision of each program code across versions. Both join to SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION via PROGRAM_CODE = CIP_PROGRAM_CODE to attribute courses to CIP programs and categories.\"}], \"column_concept\": [{\"id\": \"column_concept_num_of_rooms\", \"desc\": \"NUM_OF_ROOMS columns recording how many rooms a building contains, replicated across the current and historical building tables of both families. The building-table columns hold the current room count (one value per building); the history-table columns hold the room count at each fiscal period, used for room-count statistics (average, range, variance, minimum) across a building's history records.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_assignable_area\", \"desc\": \"Assignable-area measure columns at different granularity levels and time semantics: building-level current and per-fiscal-period assignable area, floor-level assignable area, and the space-domain assignable square footage. All FCLT_*/FAC_* columns are in square meters; BUILDINGS.BLDG_ASSIGNABLE_SQUARE_FOOTAGE is in square feet. Choosing the right column determines whether the measure is a building total, a floor total, a historical value, or a space-assignment figure.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_space_unit_key\", \"desc\": \"Space unit key columns identifying the organizational space-assignment unit across the space dimension and fact tables. SPACE_UNIT_KEY is the join key linking SPACE_DETAIL room rows to space unit identity (name/code) and, through SPACE_UNIT, to the owning facilities organization.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_dlc_key\", \"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center key columns (values like 'D_AEROASTRO', 'D_IDSS', 'D_BIOLOGY') identifying a DLC across the facilities, HR, space, and academic-department domains. They are the universal cross-domain join key linking facilities organizations and space units to HR organization units, the master department hierarchy, and academic departments. Naming and completeness vary: DLC_KEY in most tables, D_CODE in MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT, DLC_CODE in the master hierarchy tables; some columns carry composite values ('D_DSL:HQ') or nulls.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_building_room\", \"desc\": \"Combined building-room identifier columns (e.g. '1-080') appearing in both the space assignment fact table and the facilities room inventory. They identify the same physical room concept but come from different business processes with different coverage and companion measures.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_department_name\", \"desc\": \"Department name columns across subject offering, catalog, lookup, employee, and library reserve instructor tables. Two academic naming conventions exist (DEPARTMENT_NAME vs OFFER_DEPT_NAME) with the same academic value domain; LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT also holds academic departments but in a 'COURSE_NUMBER - Department Name' prefixed format (e.g. '18 - Mathematics'); EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME shares the column name but holds the HR organizational unit name (different value domain). Choosing the right one depends on the table family, the value format, whether the department is the catalog owner or the actual offering department, and whether an academic or HR department is meant.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_office_location\", \"desc\": \"OFFICE_LOCATION columns recording where a person's office/desk is, replicated across the person-directory tables (SE_PERSON, MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY, EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY, DRUPAL_EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY). All hold a building or building-room text identifier in the same value domain as FCLT_ROOMS.BUILDING_ROOM, but they describe different populations (employee/person master vs student vs primary employee directory vs Drupal employee feed) and differ sharply in non-null coverage and in how many values are building-room ('BLDG-ROOM') versus building-only ('BLDG'). Choosing the right column determines whose office is reported and whether room-level joins to FCLT_ROOMS succeed.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_facility_organization_key\", \"desc\": \"Facility organization key columns attributing space units and rooms to organizations in the hierarchical organization tree. Two naming conventions exist across table families (FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY in FCLT_*/SPACE_* tables vs ORGANIZATION_KEY in FAC_* tables) with the same value domain.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_enrollment_measures\", \"desc\": \"Enrollment measure columns across subject offering, summary, textbook-program, and library tables. Two families exist: NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS (student headcount snapshots) and SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER (official registrar enrollment), at section, subject, or program scope.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_access_level\", \"desc\": \"Access level columns recorded at three granularity levels of the facilities domain plus the space-planning room feed: building-level ACCESS_LEVEL_CODE/ACCESS_LEVEL_NAME (current and per-fiscal-period history), floor-level ACCESS_LEVEL, and room-level ACCESS_LEVEL (FCLT_ROOMS, FAC_ROOMS, ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD). They share a numeric value domain (observed 0-3) but describe the access restriction of different physical objects or come from different feeds, so filters and joins must target the granularity and table family the question refers to.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_total_units\", \"desc\": \"Total credit unit columns replicated across catalog and registrar subject tables. They represent the same business quantity (total credit units of a subject) but come from different processes and pair with different companion unit columns.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_building_type_site\", \"desc\": \"Building classification columns replicated across the current and historical building tables of both table families: BUILDING_TYPE ('ACADEMIC', 'SERVICE', 'RESIDENT') and SITE ('MIT', 'BATES', 'LINC', 'BOS', etc.). They carry the same value domain but differ in time semantics: the building-table columns are the current classification, while the history-table columns are the classification recorded at each fiscal period, so filtering by one versus the other can select different building sets.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_term_code\", \"desc\": \"Term code columns in YYYYTT format (e.g. '2025FA', '2019SP', '2021JA', '2012SU'; TT = FA Fall, SP Spring, JA January/IAP, SU Summer) appearing across term dimension and fact tables. They are the universal join key linking subject offerings, textbook materials, library reserves, and IAP activities to term attributes.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_subject_id\", \"desc\": \"Subject identifier columns shared across catalog, registrar, textbook-program, and library tables. SUBJECT_ID is the cross-domain subject join key in 'CODE.NUMBER' format (e.g. '18.01'); it appears in every subject-related fact table but at different grains and program scopes.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_master_subject_id\", \"desc\": \"Master subject identifier columns (MASTER_SUBJECT_ID and its sortable variant MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT) replicated across the registrar offering tables, the subject summary, the textbook program, the library reserve program, and the CIS course catalog. For clustered subjects (e.g. joint or cross-listed offerings), the master subject identifier points to the leading subject of the cluster, so joining on it matches offerings that share the same master subject even when their own SUBJECT_ID differs. SUBJECT_ID/SUBJECT_ID_SORT identify the subject itself, while MASTER_SUBJECT_ID/MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT identify the cluster's master; the _SORT columns are the sortable forms of the same values used for cross-table joins.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_year_columns\", \"desc\": \"Year columns across term, catalog, and time dimension tables representing different year systems: academic year, fiscal year, financial aid year, and degree year. Selecting the correct year system is essential for yearly grouping and partitioning.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_fiscal_period\", \"desc\": \"Fiscal period code columns in YYYYMM format (e.g. '199602' = FY1996 period 2, '201505') appearing in two distinct roles: as the primary key of the month-grain time dimension (TIME_MONTH.FISCAL_PERIOD, also mirrored in TIME_DAY.FISCAL_PERIOD for day-to-month linkage), and as the snapshot-period stamp of the facilities historical tables (FCLT_BUILDING_HIST, FCLT_BUILDING_HIST_1, FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS_HIST, FCLT_FLOOR_HIST, FCLT_ROOMS_HIST, FCLT_MAJOR_USE_HIST). Both roles share the same YYYYMM value domain, but the time dimension uses it for calendar grouping while the history tables use it to mark when a facilities snapshot was taken.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_material_status_key\", \"desc\": \"Material status key columns of the textbook program (TIP) and library reserve program. Both are coded status references decoded by their own lookup tables (key value equals code value), with independent value domains: TIP statuses ('RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options, 'RC' Recommended, 'PC' Val-u option, 'BR' Bookstore recommends, 'CL' Go to class first, 'NM' Course has no materials, 'U' Unknown, plus NULL-description keys) vs library reserve statuses ('U' Unknown, 'R' null description, 'N' Non-Required Course Material, 'O' Reserve only, 'X' No Required Textbook, 'Y' Required Course Material).\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_hass_attribute\", \"desc\": \"HASS (Humanities, Arts, and Social Sciences) attribute code and description columns. The code columns appear in the three course catalog feeds and in the CIS_HASS_ATTRIBUTE lookup; description columns exist in three variants: the catalog-embedded HASS_ATTRIBUTE_DESC, the lookup's DESCRIPTION_ON_FORM (registration-form wording), and DESCRIPTION_IN_BULLETIN (short bulletin wording). Selecting the right description variant depends on the wording requested by the question.\"}]}}"
    },
    {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_a7cd6b6bfef543dbba848a22",
      "name": "semantic_get",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"entities\": [{\"id\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION\", \"name\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION\", \"desc\": \"Facilities organization dimension table: one row per organization in the institute's hierarchical organization tree (levels 1-6, from institute-wide down to sub-units), with organization identifiers and names, parent and major-organization attribution, hierarchy level, assignable-space flag, course number for academic departments, description, DLC (department/lab/center) key and name, and cross-references to HR organization units. Parent of SPACE_UNIT (space assigned to organizations) and referenced by FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY for room occupancy attribution.\", \"columns\": {\"FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Surrogate key of the facilities organization; joins to SPACE_UNIT.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY and FCLT_ROOMS.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY\"}, \"ORGANIZATION_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Organization identifier (same value as the organization key in current data)\"}, \"ORGANIZATION\": {\"desc\": \"Short organization abbreviation, e.g. 'AERO', 'ADMISS'\"}, \"ORGANIZATION_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Display name of the organization, e.g. 'AERO & ASTRO'; used for organization-name reporting\"}, \"FCLT_ORG_PARENT_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Key of the parent organization in the hierarchy tree; null for the top-level organization\"}, \"ORG_PARENT\": {\"desc\": \"Abbreviation of the parent organization, e.g. 'S ENG' (School of Engineering)\"}, \"FCLT_MAJOR_ORG_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Key of the major (top-level grouping) organization this organization rolls up to\"}, \"MAJOR_ORG\": {\"desc\": \"Abbreviation of the major organization, e.g. 'PROVST', 'CHNCLR'\"}, \"ORGANIZATION_LEVEL\": {\"desc\": \"Level of the organization in the hierarchy tree (1 = institute-wide root, 2-4 = intermediate divisions/schools, 5 = department/DLC level, 6 = sub-organization); stored as string, filter with values like '5'\"}, \"ORGANIZATION_NUMBER\": {\"desc\": \"Official organization number used in administrative systems\"}, \"ORGANIZATION_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sortable hierarchical organization code reflecting the tree path\"}, \"ASSIGNABLE\": {\"desc\": \"Flag ('1'/'0') indicating whether the organization is an assignable-space organizational unit\"}, \"COURSE\": {\"desc\": \"Academic course (department) number for degree-granting academic departments, e.g. '16' for Aeronautics and Astronautics; null for non-academic organizations\"}, \"DESCRIPTION\": {\"desc\": \"Long description of the organization, e.g. 'Department of Aeronautics and Astronautics'; null for many non-academic organizations\"}, \"WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"ETL warehouse load date\"}, \"DLC_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center key, e.g. 'D_AEROASTRO'; joins to FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY.DLC_KEY, HR_ORG_UNIT.DLC_KEY (for HR org unit title/level and HR department attributes; may fan out when a DLC maps to multiple HR org units), and MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY.DLC_KEY (for the standard department hierarchy path)\"}, \"DLC_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center full name, e.g. 'Aeronautics and Astronautics'\"}, \"HR_DEPARTMENT_CODE_OLD\": {\"desc\": \"Legacy HR department code cross-reference\"}, \"HR_ORG_UNIT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"HR organization unit identifier cross-reference; links to HR_ORG_UNIT\"}, \"HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Department name as recorded in HR systems\"}}, \"default_granularity\": \"one row per facilities organization\"}, {\"id\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT\", \"name\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT\", \"desc\": \"HR organization unit dimension table: one row per HR organization unit with unit key/ID/title, unit level classification (ALL MIT, TOP LEVEL, DEPARTMENTS, SUB DEPARTMENT, ORGANIZATION LEVEL, NON HIERARCHY ORG UNITS), HR department identifiers and name variants (short, long, alphabetical), organization hierarchy area names (school area, top level, root), the full HR hierarchy path levels 1-7 (each with ID, sort order, and name), and DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME cross-references to departments/labs/centers. Joined from FCLT_ORGANIZATION and MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY via DLC_KEY to attach HR department attributes (title, level, department name, long name, hierarchy path) to facilities organizations and DLCs; a single DLC_KEY can map to multiple HR org unit rows, so joins via DLC_KEY may fan out.\", \"columns\": {\"HR_ORG_UNIT_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Surrogate key of the HR organization unit, formatted 'O' + numeric ID (e.g. 'O10000333'); joins to HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW.HR_ORG_UNIT_KEY\"}, \"HR_ORG_UNIT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Numeric HR organization unit identifier (e.g. '10000333'); cross-referenced by FCLT_ORGANIZATION.HR_ORG_UNIT_ID\"}, \"HR_ORG_UNIT_TITLE\": {\"desc\": \"Title of the HR organization unit, e.g. 'Institute for Data, Systems, and Society'; reported as the HR org unit title of a facilities organization joined via DLC_KEY\"}, \"HR_ORG_UNIT_LEVEL\": {\"desc\": \"Level classification of the HR organization unit; observed values: 'ALL MIT', 'TOP LEVEL', 'DEPARTMENTS', 'SUB DEPARTMENT', 'ORGANIZATION LEVEL', 'NON HIERARCHY ORG UNITS', and null; distinct from the numeric ORGANIZATION_LEVEL of FCLT_ORGANIZATION\"}, \"HR_DEPARTMENT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Numeric HR department identifier (same value as HR_ORG_UNIT_ID in current data); absent from HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW\"}, \"HR_DEPARTMENT_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"HR department code in 'HR-NNNNNN' format, e.g. 'HR-068100'\"}, \"HR_DEPARTMENT_CODE_OLD\": {\"desc\": \"Legacy HR department code (numeric part of HR_DEPARTMENT_CODE), e.g. '68100'\"}, \"HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"HR department name, e.g. 'Institute for Data, Systems, and Society'; the HR-side counterpart of academic department names, used for grouping/partitioning organizations by HR department\"}, \"HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME_LONG\": {\"desc\": \"Long form of the HR department name (often identical to HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME)\"}, \"HR_DEPARTMENT_NAME_ALPHA\": {\"desc\": \"Alphabetical-sort variant of the HR department name\"}, \"ORG_HIER_SCHOOL_AREA_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Name of the school/area the unit belongs to in the organization hierarchy, e.g. 'Schwarzman College of Computing Area', 'VP for Finance Area'\"}, \"ORG_HIER_TOP_LEVEL_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Name of the top-level area of the unit in the organization hierarchy, e.g. 'Provost Area', 'Executive Vice President Area'\"}, \"ORG_HIER_ROOT_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Root name of the organization hierarchy, 'MIT-All' for all rows\"}, \"HR_ORG_LEVEL1_ID\": {\"desc\": \"ID of the level-1 node (institute root, '10000000') in the HR organization hierarchy path\"}, \"HR_ORG_LEVEL1_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sort order of the level-1 node in the HR hierarchy path\"}, \"HR_ORG_LEVEL1_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Name of the level-1 node, 'MIT-All'\"}, \"HR_ORG_LEVEL2_ID\": {\"desc\": \"ID of the level-2 node in the HR organization hierarchy path\"}, \"HR_ORG_LEVEL2_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sort order of the level-2 node in the HR hierarchy path\"}, \"HR_ORG_LEVEL2_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Name of the level-2 node, e.g. 'Provost Area', 'Executive Vice President Area'\"}, \"HR_ORG_LEVEL3_ID\": {\"desc\": \"ID of the level-3 node in the HR organization hierarchy path\"}, \"HR_ORG_LEVEL3_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sort order of the level-3 node in the HR hierarchy path\"}, \"HR_ORG_LEVEL3_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Name of the level-3 node, e.g. a school/VP area name\"}, \"HR_ORG_LEVEL4_ID\": {\"desc\": \"ID of the level-4 node in the HR organization hierarchy path\"}, \"HR_ORG_LEVEL4_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sort order of the level-4 node in the HR hierarchy path\"}, \"HR_ORG_LEVEL4_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Name of the level-4 node, e.g. an area/office name\"}, \"HR_ORG_LEVEL5_ID\": {\"desc\": \"ID of the level-5 node in the HR organization hierarchy path\"}, \"HR_ORG_LEVEL5_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sort order of the level-5 node in the HR hierarchy path\"}, \"HR_ORG_LEVEL5_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Name of the level-5 node, e.g. a department/unit name\"}, \"HR_ORG_LEVEL6_ID\": {\"desc\": \"ID of the level-6 node in the HR organization hierarchy path; null when the path is shallower; absent from HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW\"}, \"HR_ORG_LEVEL6_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sort order of the level-6 node; absent from HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW\"}, \"HR_ORG_LEVEL6_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Name of the level-6 node; absent from HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW\"}, \"HR_ORG_LEVEL7_ID\": {\"desc\": \"ID of the level-7 (deepest) node in the HR organization hierarchy path; absent from HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW\"}, \"HR_ORG_LEVEL7_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sort order of the level-7 node; absent from HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW\"}, \"HR_ORG_LEVEL7_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Name of the level-7 node; absent from HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW\"}, \"DLC_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center key cross-reference, e.g. 'D_IDSS', 'D_OTP'; joins to FCLT_ORGANIZATION.DLC_KEY and MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY.DLC_KEY; null for units without a DLC assignment, and one DLC_KEY may appear on multiple HR org unit rows\"}, \"DLC_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center full name cross-reference, e.g. 'Office of Treasury and Planning'; may differ from the HR unit title; carried only by HR_ORG_UNIT (not HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW); can be used for name-based self-matching of units sharing a DLC\"}, \"WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"ETL warehouse load date\"}}, \"default_granularity\": \"one row per HR organization unit\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_dlc_key\", \"name\": \"DLC Key (Department/Lab/Center)\", \"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center key columns (values like 'D_AEROASTRO', 'D_IDSS', 'D_BIOLOGY') identifying a DLC across the facilities, HR, space, and academic-department domains. They are the universal cross-domain join key linking facilities organizations and space units to HR organization units, the master department hierarchy, and academic departments. Naming and completeness vary: DLC_KEY in most tables, D_CODE in MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT, DLC_CODE in the master hierarchy tables; some columns carry composite values ('D_DSL:HQ') or nulls.\", \"columns\": [\"FCLT_ORGANIZATION.DLC_KEY\", \"FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY.DLC_KEY\", \"HR_ORG_UNIT.DLC_KEY\", \"HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW.DLC_KEY\", \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY.DLC_KEY\", \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS.DLC_KEY\", \"MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT.D_CODE\", \"SPACE_UNIT.DLC_KEY\", \"SPACE_UNIT2.DLC_KEY\", \"SIS_DEPARTMENT.DLC_KEY\", \"SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE.DEPT_NAMES\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Naming convention\", \"detail\": \"DLC_KEY is used by FCLT_ORGANIZATION, FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY, HR_ORG_UNIT, HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW, MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY, MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS, SPACE_UNIT, SPACE_UNIT2, and SIS_DEPARTMENT; MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT names the same value domain D_CODE (with PARENT_D_CODE for the parent); MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY/LINKS additionally carry DLC_CODE holding the same value as DLC_KEY; SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE names it DEPT_NAMES despite holding DLC key values, not department names.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Uniqueness and fan-out behavior\", \"detail\": \"In MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY the DLC_KEY is unique per DLC (one row per DLC); in HR_ORG_UNIT one DLC_KEY may appear on multiple HR org unit rows (join fans out); in FCLT_ORGANIZATION multiple organizations can share a DLC_KEY; in FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY it is an assignment bridge where non-null values mark organizations with a DLC assignment; in SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE multiple supervisors can share the same DEPT_NAMES value, so joining DEPT_NAMES = DLC_KEY fans out on both sides.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Nullability and value format\", \"detail\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT.DLC_KEY is null for units without a DLC assignment (133 of 641 rows); HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW.DLC_KEY and SPACE_UNIT.DLC_KEY may contain composite values like 'D_DSL:HQ' that do not match plain DLC keys; SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE.DEPT_NAMES holds a comma-separated list of DLC keys when DEPT_COUNT > 1 (e.g. 'D_IDSS,D_LIDS'), so only single-department rows match a plain DLC key join; SIS_DEPARTMENT.DLC_KEY is populated for all 122 department rows.\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Companion name column\", \"detail\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION, HR_ORG_UNIT, and MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY carry a DLC_NAME alongside the key; SPACE_UNIT/SPACE_UNIT2, FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY, HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW, SIS_DEPARTMENT, and SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE carry only the key, so DLC name reporting requires joining one of the name-carrying tables.\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Attaching HR department attributes (unit title, department name/code, level) to a facilities organization\": \"Join FCLT_ORGANIZATION.DLC_KEY = HR_ORG_UNIT.DLC_KEY; expect possible row fan-out when a DLC maps to multiple HR org units.\", \"Reporting the DLC name of an organization or space unit\": \"Use FCLT_ORGANIZATION.DLC_KEY (carries DLC_NAME) or join HR_ORG_UNIT/MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY for DLC_NAME; SPACE_UNIT/SPACE_UNIT2 keys alone have no name column.\", \"Restricting analysis to DLCs placed in the standard department hierarchy or reporting their hierarchy path\": \"Join on MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY.DLC_KEY; use MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT.D_CODE for the same value domain when only the direct parent is needed.\", \"Filtering organizations that have a DLC assignment before DLC-level room statistics\": \"Use FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY.DLC_KEY IS NOT NULL as the assignment filter, then join FCLT_ORGANIZATION.\", \"Linking an academic department to its facilities organization or HR unit\": \"Use SIS_DEPARTMENT.DLC_KEY = FCLT_ORGANIZATION.DLC_KEY (or HR_ORG_UNIT.DLC_KEY); all SIS_DEPARTMENT rows carry a DLC key.\", \"Attributing supervisor space-usage statistics (supervisees, square footage, research volume) to a DLC or space unit\": \"Join SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE.DEPT_NAMES = SPACE_UNIT.DLC_KEY (or another DLC_KEY column); despite its name, DEPT_NAMES holds DLC key values, and only single-department rows (DEPT_COUNT = 1) match a plain DLC key.\"}}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_department_name\", \"name\": \"Department Name\", \"desc\": \"Department name columns across subject offering, catalog, lookup, employee, and library reserve instructor tables. Two academic naming conventions exist (DEPARTMENT_NAME vs OFFER_DEPT_NAME) with the same academic value domain; LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT also holds academic departments but in a 'COURSE_NUMBER - Department Name' prefixed format (e.g. '18 - Mathematics'); EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME shares the column name but holds the HR organizational unit name (different value domain). Choosing the right one depends on the table family, the value format, whether the department is the catalog owner or the actual offering department, and whether an academic or HR department is meant.\", \"columns\": [\"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME\", \"SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT\", \"MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME\", \"SE_PERSON.ORGANIZATION\"], \"comparisons\": [{\"dimension\": \"Naming convention\", \"detail\": \"DEPARTMENT_NAME is used by catalog/summary tables (COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_SUMMARY), department/course lookup tables, and the student directory (MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY); OFFER_DEPT_NAME is used by offering/program tables (SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED) and denotes the department that actually offers the subject; LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR uses the plain column name DEPARTMENT for the course's academic department; SE_PERSON uses ORGANIZATION for the person's organizational unit\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Value format\", \"detail\": \"Catalog, summary, offering, student-directory, and lookup tables store plain department names (e.g. 'Mathematics', 'Chemistry', 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'); LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT stores a 'COURSE_NUMBER - Department Name' prefixed format (e.g. '18 - Mathematics', '06 - Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'), with some unprefixed values (e.g. 'Architecture'), so it is not directly comparable to plain-name columns without stripping the prefix\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Academic vs HR/organization value domain\", \"detail\": \"Catalog, summary, offering, library, student-directory, and lookup tables share the academic department domain; EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME is the HR organizational unit name and has a different domain (e.g. 'Lincoln Laboratory', 'Department of Physics'), where some values coincide with academic names but many do not, and some carry a 'Department of ...' prefix; SE_PERSON.ORGANIZATION holds organizational unit names that may use different naming variants than the academic domain for the same unit (e.g. 'Electrical Engineering-Computer Science' vs the academic 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci'), so equality filters across the two conventions must use each table's own variant\"}, {\"dimension\": \"Companion code column\", \"detail\": \"Catalog/summary tables carry DEPARTMENT_CODE joining SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE; offering/program tables carry OFFER_DEPT_CODE joining SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE or STUDENT_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE; MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY carries DEPARTMENT (the academic department code) joining SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE, which is the reliable join key instead of the name; LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR has no department code column, only the prefixed name text; EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY carries DEPARTMENT_NUMBER (HR department number) and SE_PERSON carries no department code, neither joining to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\"}], \"decision_guide\": {\"Filtering subjects by department in catalog or summary analysis\": \"Use COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.DEPARTMENT_NAME or SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME.\", \"Filtering by department in section-level, textbook-program, or library analysis\": \"Use the OFFER_DEPT_NAME column of SUBJECT_OFFERED / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY / TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED / LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.\", \"Joining fact tables to department dimension attributes (school, full name, degree-granting)\": \"Prefer code joins: DEPARTMENT_CODE / OFFER_DEPT_CODE = SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE; name equality joins are used when codes are unavailable.\", \"Matching departments across a DEPARTMENT_NAME table and an OFFER_DEPT_NAME table\": \"The values are directly comparable (same academic name domain), e.g. joining SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME to TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_NAME.\", \"Filtering employees by their HR organizational unit (e.g. names containing 'Department', or HR units like 'Political Science')\": \"Use EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME; do not join it to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE, and pair it with DEPARTMENT_NUMBER for HR grouping.\", \"Filtering by department in section-level, textbook-program, or library subject analysis\": \"Use the OFFER_DEPT_NAME column of SUBJECT_OFFERED / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY / TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED / LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.\", \"Filtering library reserve course instructors by academic department or library unit\": \"Use LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT with the prefixed value format (e.g. '18 - Mathematics'); do not compare it directly to plain department-name columns.\", \"Filtering students by their academic department\": \"Use MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT (code) joined to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE for reliable matching, or MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME for direct name filters; the name shares the academic domain with SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME.\", \"Filtering a person master (SE_PERSON) record by organizational unit such as an academic department\": \"Use SE_PERSON.ORGANIZATION with its own naming variant (e.g. 'Electrical Engineering-Computer Science'); do not equate it directly to MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME or SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME, which use the academic variant (e.g. 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci').\"}}], \"not_found\": []}"
    },
